{"title":"2001 USA TST Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Zuming Feng</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a finite set of positive integers. Prove that there exists \na finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/3254647aba215297c432d4a99a5a72b6f45fcbdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\subseteq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae35686a609764f4a2cbf4dfc36383faf5f00919.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{x\\in B} x = \\sum_{x\\in B} x^2.\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma 1.</b> For any finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers, there exists a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb14cf6e75ab537cda755df75ef142e844d72d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\subseteq C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e3de622ffca880dfd805184a0075137f5bc6c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{x \\in C} x \\ge \\sum_{x\\in C} x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"111\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  Let us abbreviate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/5/e35e049e634d152728435d15565f4ee86d22ed40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\prod_{x\\in A}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f747e0395f311fcc903bf8299db32049ab51cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\sum_{x\\in A} x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"79\" height=\"39\" />.  Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65c562ae0f07e8800e21c6c8c0a74fd5cea88e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &lt; s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> (otherwise, we may have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848a04faeeabaf1ca62a4081460b017bf225f991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />).  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4291c193a57f20f62a578e1db31614adeac4b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(s,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> (and thus larger than any element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />).  Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcba29d901d1dbea55bd949194649a814c7079cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = A \\cup \\{a, a+1, a+2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, evidently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb14cf6e75ab537cda755df75ef142e844d72d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\subseteq C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bd34a5b8be56d7b07402b75002a5afa7d261a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\prod_{x\\in C} x &amp;= pa(a+1)(a+2) &gt; pa (a+1)^2 &gt; 5(a+1)^2 \\\\ &amp;&gt; s + a^2 + (a+1)^2 + (a+2)^2 = \\sum_{x \\in C} x, \\end{align*}\" width=\"392\" height=\"87\" />\nas desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2.</b> For any finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e3de622ffca880dfd805184a0075137f5bc6c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{x \\in C} x \\ge \\sum_{x\\in C} x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"111\" height=\"39\" />, there exists a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69a7a7bce37c3d65355aeed0c45769016f4721dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\subseteq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f080ba163c4a3c3c3ed33731db6dc431cfb736c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{x\\in B}x = \\sum_{x\\in B} x^2 .\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  Let us abbreviate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f4eaef8a5f0f7721fc0bb2114af1a478af0192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\sum_{x \\in C}x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"79\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f7d8d9fee2afe9e1d5215867c15dd4e1012b699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\prod_{x \\in C} x - \\sum_{x \\in C} x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"142\" height=\"39\" />.  We induct on the quantity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which by hypothesis is a nonnegative integer.\n</p><p>For our base case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791662898215b138613f4dada0a3ce54193d735f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, we may take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf7026c16cd53bd4c951c73249436b4efcf0f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now suppose that the lemma holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d196a69b8d351d3a0202c644980f232f357bbffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.  Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da6365830ca59e4466e591afa31cd9bb47bb8f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=k$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc0efeeeecff97b22791131de1c4f3e9be16f683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39; = C \\cup \\{s+k-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/31696879fdb3b4672303330c86c8797d25da31eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{x\\in C&#39;} x - \\sum_{x\\in C&#39;}x^2 = (s+k)(s+k-1) - s - (s+k-1)^2 = k-1,\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"39\" />\nso by inductive hypothesis, there exists a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12ad4736b1ba5dc530f378846e294f411ff0458a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39; \\subseteq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb7f4fa9f5d502cc90211ef48e9412d9f9cf21cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{x\\in B} x = \\sum_{x\\in B} x^2 .\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f77954629d3594e3ffbf696b002357b0926f7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\subseteq C&#39; \\subseteq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />, this set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies the lemma's conditions.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Combining the statments of Lemmata 1 and 2, we are done.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 USA TST Problems (page does not exist)\">2001 USA TST Problems</a></li>\n<li>&lt;url&gt;Forum/viewtopic.php?t=24756 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017111720\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 215/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 356/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7424/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.752      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    6.752      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6773:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017111720 and revision id 25216. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}